course: dictionary
lesson: 15941
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on where they are used. Unsettled is one of these. It is built from settle, which means calm or sorted, and un-, which means not. So unsettled means not calm, not finished, or not steady. Which meaning fits depends on the context.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The forecast says unsettled weather on Saturday» is about the sky, so it means the weather will keep changing. «Mia felt unsettled on her first day» is about a feeling, so it means she was worried and not calm. The clues show which meaning to use.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. If you read «The phone bill is still unsettled» and think of unpaid, the sentence makes sense: the bill still needs paying. If your meaning does not fit, try another one from the list.
fact: Unsettled is an adjective, which describes a noun.
fact: «Unsettled» can mean changing often, with rain and wind likely, when talking about weather.
fact: «Unsettled» can mean worried, nervous or not calm, when talking about people.
fact: «Unsettled» can mean not yet decided, like an argument, or not yet paid, like a bill.
fact: «Unsettled» can also be the past form of the verb unsettle: «The noise unsettled the dog» means it made the dog feel worried.
exercise: «The forecast says unsettled weather on Saturday.» What does unsettled mean here? | *Changing, with rain and wind likely | Very hot and dry | Calm and sunny all day | Finished and sorted out
exercise: «Mia felt unsettled on her first day at her new school.» What does unsettled mean? | *Worried and not calm | Happy and relaxed | Very excited to finish | Not yet paid
exercise: «The phone bill is still unsettled.» What does unsettled mean in this sentence? | Changing often | Made someone feel worried | Sorted out and done | *Not yet paid
test: «The class vote is still unsettled.» What does unsettled mean? | Cold and wet | Very noisy | Finished and counted | *Not yet decided
test: «The noise unsettled the baby.» What does unsettled mean here? | *Made the baby feel worried | Stopped the noise | Made the baby sleepy | Gave the baby a hug
exam: Jayden says unsettled always means worried. What is the right answer? | No, it means very happy | Yes, but only at school | Yes, it always means worried | *No, it can mean changing weather, an undecided matter or an unpaid bill
